
Compile/Build 
=============

1) Compiling under Linux
------------------------
$ autoreconf -i
$ ./configure
$ make


2) Cross-Compiling under Linux, for Windows
-------------------------------------------
$ ./configure  --host=i586-pc-mingw32
(or, to use static linking, which does not require installing any mingw dll's on windows)
$ ./configure  --host=i586-pc-mingw32 LDFLAGS="-static"
$ make





3) Cross-Compiling for Windows with Docker
------------------------------------------
Builds a static 32-bit iec2c.exe into ./dist-win/. Run from the matiec root.

PowerShell : docker build -t matiec-mingw docker; docker run --rm -v "${PWD}:/src" -v "${PWD}/dist-win:/out" matiec-mingw
Linux/macOS: docker build -t matiec-mingw docker && docker run --rm -v "$PWD:/src" -v "$PWD/dist-win:/out" matiec-mingw
Git Bash   : as Linux, but prefix the 'docker run' with MSYS_NO_PATHCONV=1

The image build is only needed once. Sources are copied into the container,
so a native build in the same tree keeps its Makefile and object files.


Maintaining the Build Environment
=================================
-> Add new files to Makefile.am or add a new makefile
$ autoreconf


-> Prepare clean project
$ make distclean



-> Remember to add these files to your .hgignore
	Makefile
	config.*
	*.a
	.deps


